{"id":"02bd3255-8e82-4774-8a40-b03d8896cda7","updated_at":"2026-06-09T22:39:01.935Z","updated_by":"3185519865","created_at":"2026-05-29T21:48:48.887Z","created_by":"3185519865","name":"C2 Beaconing Pattern","tags":["network","C2","beaconing","T1071"],"interval":"4h","enabled":true,"revision":17,"description":"Fires when the same source-destination IP pair generates 1000+ connections within a 4-hour window. Indicates potential automated beaconing behavior consistent with C2 communication.","risk_score":47,"severity":"medium","note":"- Identify destination AS organization — Microsoft, Google, Amazon, Apple, Cloudflare suggest legitimate services\n\n- Check time-of-day pattern — 24/7 consistent beaconing is more suspicious than business-hours-only\n\n- Calculate interval consistency — if intervals are tightly clustered (e.g., every 28-32 seconds), beaconing is highly likely\n\n- Check connection size — small consistent bytes per connection (<1KB) suggests check-in, larger consistent suggests data transfer\n\n- Look for jitter — sophisticated C2 adds random jitter to evade detection; perfectly regular intervals are simpler malware or legit polling\n","license":"","output_index":"","meta":{"kibana_siem_app_url":"https://prime-one.kb.us-west-2.aws.found.io/s/sm_soc_analysts/app/security"},"investigation_fields":{"field_names":["pulse_meta.location_name","pulse_meta.orgs.name"]},"author":[],"false_positives":[],"from":"now-245m","rule_id":"1994e184-3606-4b93-8c31-7dbed01e0c42","max_signals":500,"risk_score_mapping":[],"severity_mapping":[],"threat":[{"framework":"MITRE ATT&CK","tactic":{"id":"TA0011","name":"Command and Control","reference":"https://attack.mitre.org/tactics/TA0011/"},"technique":[{"id":"T1071","name":"Application Layer Protocol","reference":"https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1071/","subtechnique":[]}]}],"to":"now","references":[],"version":1,"exceptions_list":[{"id":"70af909c-ce55-49b6-9b01-f7ed7b0879e6","list_id":"3d4c2db2-177c-4e03-aef0-84497352e639","type":"rule_default","namespace_type":"single"},{"id":"90d851ef-9852-4ec0-8937-a46446c262f8","list_id":"7edf230c-6eaa-4958-9101-662cf59f9764","type":"detection","namespace_type":"single"},{"id":"62f618da-b345-4486-8e5f-0946d47f903e","list_id":"a7a09c40-fc17-49d4-ab67-bc0b25af1274","type":"detection","namespace_type":"single"}],"immutable":false,"rule_source":{"type":"internal"},"related_integrations":[],"required_fields":[],"setup":"Expected volume: Moderate (10-30 alerts/day after tuning)\nTrue positive: Implant beaconing to C2 — Cobalt Strike, Empire, Sliver, custom malware\nKnown false positives: (1) Software update services (Windows Update endpoints, Apple Software Update, vendor updaters). (2) Streaming services (Spotify, YouTube background). (3) Backup applications. (4) Telemetry from anti-virus and EDR products. (5) CDN endpoints serving popular sites.\n","type":"threshold","language":"kuery","index":["logs-kinesis-*"],"query":"source.routable: false AND destination.routable: true AND NOT destination.as.organization.name: (\"GOOGLE\" OR \"AMAZON\" OR \"MICROSOFT\" OR \"CLOUDFLARE\" OR \"AKAMAI\" OR \"FASTLY\" OR \"APPLE\" OR \"Cisco OpenDNS, LLC\" OR \"DNSFilter, Inc.\" OR \"Datto, LLC\" OR \"Akamai International B.V.\")","filters":[],"threshold":{"field":["source.ip","destination.ip"],"value":1000,"cardinality":[]},"alert_suppression":{"duration":{"value":8,"unit":"h"}},"actions":[]}
